Q: How does typeid work for polymorphic/non-polymorphic types? A: <p>I suspect the code should have had:</p>
<pre><code>extern Decider* d;

int main()
{
    char const* name = typeid(*d).name();
    return (int)sizeof(*d);
} 
</code></pre>
<p>That would have better expressed their point, in my opinion.</p>
<p>(I have that book.  Your transciption of the code is accurate.  I think the book's example could be improved.)</p>
